[{:db/id "q-122504/selection/0826537a88ea94ddca6c2c6326e79053888610ec2f67898650670e46e49b6d0d" :answer/id #uuid "dbb72288-83f4-59ac-9ad4-8945758a6ea9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122504/selection/f25b97839ea3e4bb401ff0ba78de28404b73b63f071bcdc1a778b24463827341" :answer/id #uuid "77285a09-7234-5603-bee4-f071b99ce370" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-5)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122504/selection/2aad3963b88cfb545d755ac23e77e5662d28c4c5dd583174ef320dbbf24ba354" :answer/id #uuid "a255bb03-b6aa-58ea-9b20-ee91c04fc360" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-5)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122504/selection/4ec1e0c7458c86f5d6bb4fb56882af94ebe43d4cbdaca24ba1f357c19ef6a207" :answer/id #uuid "78ff4fbd-185e-576a-b1fd-f5b900404988" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122504/selection/2dc72d835f2537ff8f2dfab006e7d8a857035536a3d1a5141ba792f24134a9d8" :answer/id #uuid "abba55df-8ca9-525d-9810-ee4726b27692" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122504/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb1cba96-120c-54ae-b108-697966842f8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122504/selection/2dc72d835f2537ff8f2dfab006e7d8a857035536a3d1a5141ba792f24134a9d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-122504/selection/0826537a88ea94ddca6c2c6326e79053888610ec2f67898650670e46e49b6d0d" "q-122504/selection/f25b97839ea3e4bb401ff0ba78de28404b73b63f071bcdc1a778b24463827341" "q-122504/selection/2aad3963b88cfb545d755ac23e77e5662d28c4c5dd583174ef320dbbf24ba354" "q-122504/selection/4ec1e0c7458c86f5d6bb4fb56882af94ebe43d4cbdaca24ba1f357c19ef6a207" "q-122504/selection/2dc72d835f2537ff8f2dfab006e7d8a857035536a3d1a5141ba792f24134a9d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122504" :question/id #uuid "768f5ade-57c0-528d-9864-4b38b9f72d0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-122504" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=xy,$ traversed once along the circle $C$ with equation $(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}=25?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $5$ centered at $(-1,0).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1,\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{sin}^{2}⁡t+25{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=xy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1)(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1)\\cdot 5\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =25{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122504/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca6cfe72-a82e-59be-b454-bcc643b3596c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122504"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-122263"] :question/problem "Which of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2},$ traversed once along the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $2$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-122509/selection/8a811571c538f5fc6bfee0b573c6c9eac4673fdb4661ae5880ea453be1fec245" :answer/id #uuid "0377f728-ce56-5c1d-b7f6-836f6d6dc584" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122509/selection/ad089e43907e431ba8f36da6995f2b1099fa2edcdf8016df8208f3a3e260d19b" :answer/id #uuid "660bd6d0-6a5a-5c88-9858-c77fcb9805ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122509/selection/887dfb6cb275071f8f2120d0d8ef4fd43cfcda9ace20d03b00e08cad8f6fe361" :answer/id #uuid "502f7bd3-b3b8-59ab-8cb3-1b60d076dd5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122509/selection/ad37e37f990bccacb4e0373772e7b9c053536ec103c4e97bd0d949cd8fa51fce" :answer/id #uuid "123894c1-ef6d-570e-8499-2dd61182c0b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122509/selection/8a8d59b6e81966f29d1784322d9bf87c15fb594f293728405493826462132b04" :answer/id #uuid "4e48e65c-224d-592c-9bfc-a6bf22f068b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122509/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a7b34be-b7be-5575-8b12-756b51a4f57c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122509/selection/8a811571c538f5fc6bfee0b573c6c9eac4673fdb4661ae5880ea453be1fec245" :answer-field/choices ["q-122509/selection/8a811571c538f5fc6bfee0b573c6c9eac4673fdb4661ae5880ea453be1fec245" "q-122509/selection/ad089e43907e431ba8f36da6995f2b1099fa2edcdf8016df8208f3a3e260d19b" "q-122509/selection/887dfb6cb275071f8f2120d0d8ef4fd43cfcda9ace20d03b00e08cad8f6fe361" "q-122509/selection/ad37e37f990bccacb4e0373772e7b9c053536ec103c4e97bd0d949cd8fa51fce" "q-122509/selection/8a8d59b6e81966f29d1784322d9bf87c15fb594f293728405493826462132b04"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122509" :question/id #uuid "01acc2c4-61a4-5484-813b-8353dc8736ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-122509" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)={y}^{3},$ traversed once along the circle $C$ with equation $(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=36?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $6$ centered at $(1,1).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1,\\,6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)j \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{sin}^{2}⁡t+36{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={y}^{3},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }((6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)^{3})\\cdot 6\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122509/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca6cfe72-a82e-59be-b454-bcc643b3596c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122509"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122540/selection/57a4c02d305afdb46f9bf45d2e2068afe9b4e20f24907cb76d2dbc432345cb19" :answer/id #uuid "f008596e-0d30-51c8-bd22-e08bb4e20a6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122540/selection/f2f7f20815c1f31d4cdd462cb84d7e3927e34d950b9b2186b6e058d38f034ecb" :answer/id #uuid "a09be9c1-a58b-525d-aa2c-541560d9d069" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-3)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122540/selection/1bcaadeb5e55c9b2055f9647c7a06ba7877bef0f35bf22a27bdf1c5a36f2b7ec" :answer/id #uuid "c93b67b4-3a94-5fea-91c6-6ed2c229336c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-3)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122540/selection/548057157d6bf82e419357102f3c5af3e6b7c12dce0ea216b6fc2c4e821db0b8" :answer/id #uuid "41452db0-144d-5b4c-8eec-4472970e5d24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122540/selection/cea3459f1ce65a0df522701687b777cb45690f08391ee36f7f9e00fb6a2ba3fc" :answer/id #uuid "e5f14c2f-6d6d-5b0b-b7e7-13ae02df4148" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122540/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c6514f7-ea9e-53f5-89fc-8fff62878658" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122540/selection/548057157d6bf82e419357102f3c5af3e6b7c12dce0ea216b6fc2c4e821db0b8" :answer-field/choices ["q-122540/selection/57a4c02d305afdb46f9bf45d2e2068afe9b4e20f24907cb76d2dbc432345cb19" "q-122540/selection/f2f7f20815c1f31d4cdd462cb84d7e3927e34d950b9b2186b6e058d38f034ecb" "q-122540/selection/1bcaadeb5e55c9b2055f9647c7a06ba7877bef0f35bf22a27bdf1c5a36f2b7ec" "q-122540/selection/548057157d6bf82e419357102f3c5af3e6b7c12dce0ea216b6fc2c4e821db0b8" "q-122540/selection/cea3459f1ce65a0df522701687b777cb45690f08391ee36f7f9e00fb6a2ba3fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122540" :question/id #uuid "0c026636-3333-5149-910a-9646132297e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-122540" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=1-{y}^{2},$ traversed once along the circle $C$ with equation $(x+3)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $1$ centered at $(-3,0).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-3)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=1-{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =1-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({cos}^{2}⁡t)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122540/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca6cfe72-a82e-59be-b454-bcc643b3596c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122540"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122489/selection/fe4e35d0f11bbf7bc0a04d3e89b9d1309c6bca5a040da2ad38bf5d39321e51b2" :answer/id #uuid "b63ec3f9-6f0f-59b2-bf1a-ec585fabb91f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(1-3{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122489/selection/b4370f1c195139dd9791e6baa54f723511bdd1717ab3d09f21991a0ad1b340c3" :answer/id #uuid "444677cb-94c0-5055-a2b3-a760b36c18b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(1-3{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122489/selection/a818898ca0e3038cf8ee9b4f02ab89f8fd2367ae9c98ba1f57a32d2f6497f0f0" :answer/id #uuid "e23a577e-9028-5aa8-9023-5c65c50720fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122489/selection/cad25847a72faad17718db9a1efaad97ecebb94f12097bb4a886eaa0b01414cd" :answer/id #uuid "9438e5a2-745c-547d-9d38-231d3a3521a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3-{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122489/selection/568584162ef76ca10a633e1d69e5f14c9286e4cb8463d93600748ee143ec3134" :answer/id #uuid "084d8872-827a-55b1-b161-c7d18688c0e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122489/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9ca0824-4056-5b7d-9bb7-be2b16b38775" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122489/selection/b4370f1c195139dd9791e6baa54f723511bdd1717ab3d09f21991a0ad1b340c3" :answer-field/choices ["q-122489/selection/fe4e35d0f11bbf7bc0a04d3e89b9d1309c6bca5a040da2ad38bf5d39321e51b2" "q-122489/selection/b4370f1c195139dd9791e6baa54f723511bdd1717ab3d09f21991a0ad1b340c3" "q-122489/selection/a818898ca0e3038cf8ee9b4f02ab89f8fd2367ae9c98ba1f57a32d2f6497f0f0" "q-122489/selection/cad25847a72faad17718db9a1efaad97ecebb94f12097bb4a886eaa0b01414cd" "q-122489/selection/568584162ef76ca10a633e1d69e5f14c9286e4cb8463d93600748ee143ec3134"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122489" :question/id #uuid "c8954060-eb74-5d21-b7ff-5405a3086ea5" :question/math-academy-id "q-122489" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=3-{y}^{2},$ traversed once along the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $3$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=3-{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3-(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =3-9{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3-9{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\cdot 3\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(1-3{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122489/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca6cfe72-a82e-59be-b454-bcc643b3596c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122489"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122578/selection/185615aca250d4469ef7c7e4a9cdd5906689c7845cdb5c6eb7d1abf0e826c5a0" :answer/id #uuid "025093c9-a121-5fbe-a441-016d472e79ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{e}^{5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122578/selection/46ddcc150e43add45a842e33b1265a500ebd36eb44a99a1bfbdee5c8b1dfa903" :answer/id #uuid "79d98dd6-9602-563a-a4f5-a70ae1cb32c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122578/selection/59d2cb123bf35fc1fa5a0f83471d12d8b2567f851a4b9b9113522d977d849182" :answer/id #uuid "7a427321-f760-5ec1-abe2-29526339598f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122578/selection/01172ada48cefbd6ea621040bc312ba0944ec2a477f28e5fe10c78ba75ff213f" :answer/id #uuid "15271314-32fe-5ce8-8e4e-3a79f99d8ef0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122578/selection/4698a031506479b46219d59afcae0e8df1b4ae20919e8592371238d0e138ea24" :answer/id #uuid "4f378851-4d40-58d8-a942-b49ce7820016" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{e}^{5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122578/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "931bf621-2168-5426-b433-28f80891e25b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122578/selection/185615aca250d4469ef7c7e4a9cdd5906689c7845cdb5c6eb7d1abf0e826c5a0" :answer-field/choices ["q-122578/selection/185615aca250d4469ef7c7e4a9cdd5906689c7845cdb5c6eb7d1abf0e826c5a0" "q-122578/selection/46ddcc150e43add45a842e33b1265a500ebd36eb44a99a1bfbdee5c8b1dfa903" "q-122578/selection/59d2cb123bf35fc1fa5a0f83471d12d8b2567f851a4b9b9113522d977d849182" "q-122578/selection/01172ada48cefbd6ea621040bc312ba0944ec2a477f28e5fe10c78ba75ff213f" "q-122578/selection/4698a031506479b46219d59afcae0e8df1b4ae20919e8592371238d0e138ea24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122578" :question/id #uuid "f6c2e787-d774-546b-90c4-c7c2c369feb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-122578" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)={e}^{x+y}$ along the quarter-circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25,$ traversed from the point $(-5,0)$ to the point $(0,-5)$ in the third quadrant?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $5$ centered at $O,$ shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057418/assets/2ec6f01ab00c17d4888dfefb37c2813139af9c412e99acd1a38680274b0f0ddd.png)\n\nThe curve $C$ can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{sin}^{2}⁡t+25{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={e}^{x+y},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={e}^{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & ={e}^{5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{e}^{5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}\\cdot 5\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{e}^{5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122578/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb008515-d668-509b-8c8a-76e892e709cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122578"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122582/selection/33caa7c3e7c35a64c10231d1f898fbfbc4652e56694541d8fe3af15c1df1968b" :answer/id #uuid "cfe70f81-6ec8-5232-af9c-33076eeeb7bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{1-36{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122582/selection/20c59238e3e08e8cc8a4121aad977d2daa4fdbc056c23f670f75658e86c2b76d" :answer/id #uuid "23609e4f-d873-564d-bf17-3c99fc6f4b40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{1-36{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122582/selection/488166874d6a65dcfa80d391e836e4b31da8d89072625a388948959170042a42" :answer/id #uuid "a702395e-05a8-5eed-826a-662c54705c8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{1-{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122582/selection/145bee9a7e98c25850fd86c35c1a6af203e0d327496bf3f53888b6786622f95c" :answer/id #uuid "bedd7e21-89b1-52a8-a4e9-bc2554afcd2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{1-6{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122582/selection/49a3483ba51f9630fb17346f51c00aaa73a11a10097a480f783379cf9acfa122" :answer/id #uuid "21e2af40-ad8f-5c20-9564-191bf02f0bb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{1-36{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122582/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e83a7f7-25de-527c-ad06-4fd140ddda37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122582/selection/49a3483ba51f9630fb17346f51c00aaa73a11a10097a480f783379cf9acfa122" :answer-field/choices ["q-122582/selection/33caa7c3e7c35a64c10231d1f898fbfbc4652e56694541d8fe3af15c1df1968b" "q-122582/selection/20c59238e3e08e8cc8a4121aad977d2daa4fdbc056c23f670f75658e86c2b76d" "q-122582/selection/488166874d6a65dcfa80d391e836e4b31da8d89072625a388948959170042a42" "q-122582/selection/145bee9a7e98c25850fd86c35c1a6af203e0d327496bf3f53888b6786622f95c" "q-122582/selection/49a3483ba51f9630fb17346f51c00aaa73a11a10097a480f783379cf9acfa122"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122582" :question/id #uuid "6b50e6e3-88d1-56d2-a993-e2318e36e7bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-122582" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x\\,{e}^{1-{y}^{2}}$ along the quarter-circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=36,$ traversed from the point $(6,0)$ to the point $(0,6)$ in the first quadrant?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $6$ centered at $O,$ shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057418/assets/c1e3332017b795ed6733a0547e6e449fdba3874f1d1e755118a0687ccaf7448c.png)\n\nThe curve $C$ can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{sin}^{2}⁡t+36{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x\\,{e}^{1-{y}^{2}},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{1-(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{1-36{sin}^{2}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{1-36{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\cdot 6\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =36{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{1-36{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122582/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb008515-d668-509b-8c8a-76e892e709cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122582"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122568/selection/363134f84db10f23659679ae2566cc60d2910ed3a6d7e96d4de3ee94b30f4daa" :answer/id #uuid "66dde6ac-a53e-5679-b41d-b70b065a8cce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122568/selection/fee3e838d804be9306088fc1045d4e8dc3d9ae5f7f8fed6e67bcb8220b94b1bc" :answer/id #uuid "4348f031-06e0-5b76-a5c1-9bf9472a3ece" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122568/selection/602697d3ad21fbda09826b6059d340e6f1f2e72d098051802f3caf94c08e56ed" :answer/id #uuid "0039ae3d-b23f-55bd-9e0a-93be7ddfc87e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122568/selection/de844aba7e70696f42a8be58144ad0baa5f046a20e731cc42ea347c75e2757e3" :answer/id #uuid "6c2f8ed3-4291-5e57-a0b9-25958e4fec76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122568/selection/26ddc49efd23047b3a07e7edffcfe95084f6aa9619c7fa2113382dc2604f0c65" :answer/id #uuid "d5848978-19e0-51bc-8df2-10f1b94c76da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122568/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f79a95e5-9407-5002-ae5d-d6dcc03c4e27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122568/selection/363134f84db10f23659679ae2566cc60d2910ed3a6d7e96d4de3ee94b30f4daa" :answer-field/choices ["q-122568/selection/363134f84db10f23659679ae2566cc60d2910ed3a6d7e96d4de3ee94b30f4daa" "q-122568/selection/fee3e838d804be9306088fc1045d4e8dc3d9ae5f7f8fed6e67bcb8220b94b1bc" "q-122568/selection/602697d3ad21fbda09826b6059d340e6f1f2e72d098051802f3caf94c08e56ed" "q-122568/selection/de844aba7e70696f42a8be58144ad0baa5f046a20e731cc42ea347c75e2757e3" "q-122568/selection/26ddc49efd23047b3a07e7edffcfe95084f6aa9619c7fa2113382dc2604f0c65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122568" :question/id #uuid "823c89b1-3eae-5e6a-ab33-4fed7bd74bba" :question/math-academy-id "q-122568" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057418/assets/761643a777650909b8c7ea5477b4fe246ac4032fe183df5d9ad5cb5e08ac1ecc.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x+y$ along a circle of radius $4,$ traversed from the point $(-4,0)$ to the point $(4,0),$ as shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $4$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x+y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 4\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122568/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb008515-d668-509b-8c8a-76e892e709cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122568"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122588/selection/46f884a880000cdfd89f47b28254c8b7cc5d9ec7fc5d956986195b8bc65e738f" :answer/id #uuid "da018880-d2bc-5549-8b6a-0e41c79c0618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122588/selection/48aa9769c57e1ffcdb1775809f405f2ce6e33f5d35957a29dbc5a159851e23ad" :answer/id #uuid "a60a5289-61a7-50d5-8e40-5027ae35eb80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122588/selection/da2dc94b88b2176fce9b271d040c02192542f15e414c92caf18a52f3a45a07e8" :answer/id #uuid "b778b2e0-185b-53af-94cc-88bdbfacdfd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122588/selection/8bd2588a8a668b2909e0e77bf8e1ad1d8c1f3c7ad475e4489a51fd65182f5b77" :answer/id #uuid "67fa64e9-4a7d-5630-b1aa-c4ec7ca9c486" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122588/selection/ae9a90ffb12041c5c216651460f848cd967fd41e8046953732797c55e0afedba" :answer/id #uuid "852a4ed4-cb6b-5412-8af9-f822fcd3f67d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122588/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "271c59af-7cac-58cd-9f46-dc748c9bfe99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122588/selection/48aa9769c57e1ffcdb1775809f405f2ce6e33f5d35957a29dbc5a159851e23ad" :answer-field/choices ["q-122588/selection/46f884a880000cdfd89f47b28254c8b7cc5d9ec7fc5d956986195b8bc65e738f" "q-122588/selection/48aa9769c57e1ffcdb1775809f405f2ce6e33f5d35957a29dbc5a159851e23ad" "q-122588/selection/da2dc94b88b2176fce9b271d040c02192542f15e414c92caf18a52f3a45a07e8" "q-122588/selection/8bd2588a8a668b2909e0e77bf8e1ad1d8c1f3c7ad475e4489a51fd65182f5b77" "q-122588/selection/ae9a90ffb12041c5c216651460f848cd967fd41e8046953732797c55e0afedba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122588" :question/id #uuid "b42e9373-4893-5f93-a4eb-1c63f18b5e00" :question/math-academy-id "q-122588" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x\\,\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}$ along the quarter-circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9,$ traversed from the point $(0,-3)$ to the point $(3,0)$ in the fourth quadrant?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $3$ centered at $O,$ shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057418/assets/b7c2c6f9e50988629007a06213cb3acf0a48f9951f026fb70d5a986b760abdfe.png)\n\nThe curve $C$ can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x\\,\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{9-(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{9-9{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =9{cos}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\,\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }9{cos}^{2}⁡t\\cdot 3\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =27{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122588/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb008515-d668-509b-8c8a-76e892e709cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122588"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122570/selection/2a45cc026a4445a629fc0dbbeb003603da739260d850e5aff1897177d005a196" :answer/id #uuid "96054743-b3fd-5c1f-8313-f480a9f08b4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122570/selection/a6e11117194fbfd8796e13a65e72e8f7b76bcccabf2a2a4a021c5763e0d5dd35" :answer/id #uuid "ba040e42-4fc3-5eee-b9ca-3f56113ce05e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122570/selection/57258cba89c88e1d6f67a0210d74b32e1909a5c049af5690810cea7ee780ce61" :answer/id #uuid "56b5526e-8522-5782-9964-ea88b6402f38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122570/selection/13b2ef779b94a9cfe14b9749958b71cf7774db1861c4413025fcf8be72ea9189" :answer/id #uuid "55daff39-4782-54dd-9c47-d43149c24a29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122570/selection/86015d9bcd25a698d5f78a25d1a9ed04e6863dbe17b26410ee8381dbe6c01cac" :answer/id #uuid "f4afc315-64fd-57bb-b795-ba0df6a580ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122570/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "24181d15-5737-5179-bb20-36e6d62ccbef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122570/selection/86015d9bcd25a698d5f78a25d1a9ed04e6863dbe17b26410ee8381dbe6c01cac" :answer-field/choices ["q-122570/selection/2a45cc026a4445a629fc0dbbeb003603da739260d850e5aff1897177d005a196" "q-122570/selection/a6e11117194fbfd8796e13a65e72e8f7b76bcccabf2a2a4a021c5763e0d5dd35" "q-122570/selection/57258cba89c88e1d6f67a0210d74b32e1909a5c049af5690810cea7ee780ce61" "q-122570/selection/13b2ef779b94a9cfe14b9749958b71cf7774db1861c4413025fcf8be72ea9189" "q-122570/selection/86015d9bcd25a698d5f78a25d1a9ed04e6863dbe17b26410ee8381dbe6c01cac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122570" :question/id #uuid "0e173157-70f2-508d-996b-8f564a55490d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122570" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057418/assets/4403bd230338dee226429d3f8f3ac8eaede1152aff0b6b18bd2e7ad9f3a3b8e3.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=9-{x}^{2}$ along a circle of radius $3,$ traversed from the point $(3,0)$ to the point $(0,3),$ as shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $3$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=9-{x}^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =9-(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =9-9{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =9{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}9{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot 3\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =27{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122570/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb008515-d668-509b-8c8a-76e892e709cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122585/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "83c333ce-330d-5de1-ba83-1f6ceb5dbbc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122585/selection/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce" :answer/id #uuid "dd6a74ff-a3ee-5633-984c-54de9b8d0df3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122585/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "01ed1aa1-827e-5b21-974a-2c510a7002ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122585/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "9d9bc228-688e-56b4-a722-b4ddf5775114" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122585/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "a85c214d-5b89-5302-b4f3-c25f9c5d606d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122585/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3ceaec2-92be-5d39-9923-d9a1b336e7e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122585/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-122585/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-122585/selection/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce" "q-122585/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-122585/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-122585/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122585" :question/id #uuid "3c336521-37e1-5552-8b76-3afe0c9e8b61" :question/math-academy-id "q-122585" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=xy\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1}$ along the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $3$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=xy\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\sqrt{(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+1} \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\cdot 3\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =27{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=9{sin}^{2}⁡t+1,$ $\\text{d}u=18\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{1}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122585/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c33b34e-5b57-51c1-91d0-e098364bcdfb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-122136"] :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ along the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $4$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =16{cos}^{2}⁡t-16{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =16({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =16\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }16\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\cdot 4\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =64{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=2t,$ $\\text{d}u=2\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}64{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t & =32{\\int }_{0}^{4\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =32\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{4\\pi } \\\\  & =32(0-0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-122441/selection/1eac1dfa55c44c75206716b3c0d44cb24b8ee46acd78de24e3ecacb55fec2b45" :answer/id #uuid "8145b74b-be63-5a9f-a264-3f59798f21bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122441/selection/fc5fc69f997bd1e5dc2576549008746749b84bd1570e29a4bb1bed03557c117a" :answer/id #uuid "66be6060-80cf-5421-9e4f-71adb440f026" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-{e}^{4}}{{e}^{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122441/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "1fd9e411-b4d1-5465-9536-c9d3f377fd10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122441/selection/55edc2aac16616ad04f48f9a6f6deeb2bbad759d45ec9c07ea60f281d30b0417" :answer/id #uuid "fc77084d-14fe-54cb-b004-572d952a2b57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4{e}^{4}-4}{{e}^{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122441/selection/6f8ea30af4d0b3ae382515382f511d25a5c1c31e8cfa1a734e0d71a4f3e5c0fe" :answer/id #uuid "80f0cb5c-3602-5ae9-9316-803822220bd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2+4{e}^{7}}{{e}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122441/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "01356ccf-ffaa-5d0b-b847-2a2b4c167823" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122441/selection/55edc2aac16616ad04f48f9a6f6deeb2bbad759d45ec9c07ea60f281d30b0417" :answer-field/choices ["q-122441/selection/1eac1dfa55c44c75206716b3c0d44cb24b8ee46acd78de24e3ecacb55fec2b45" "q-122441/selection/fc5fc69f997bd1e5dc2576549008746749b84bd1570e29a4bb1bed03557c117a" "q-122441/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-122441/selection/55edc2aac16616ad04f48f9a6f6deeb2bbad759d45ec9c07ea60f281d30b0417" "q-122441/selection/6f8ea30af4d0b3ae382515382f511d25a5c1c31e8cfa1a734e0d71a4f3e5c0fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122441" :question/id #uuid "86c4e485-7c50-5624-b574-a3d3f04e4c55" :question/math-academy-id "q-122441" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057418/assets/e27774d260c053a7835b30e62c2d4b41be4b8dc22efcba8f7aa95704590561cf.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y-3}$ along the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16,$ traversed from the point $(0,-4)$ to the point $(4,0),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $4$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as  \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y-3},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-3}\\cdot 4\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-3,$ $\\text{d}u=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-3}\\,\\text{d}t & =4{\\int }_{-7}^{-3}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\,{e}^{u}{|}_{-7}^{-3} \\\\  & =4({e}^{-3}-{e}^{-7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{e}^{3}}-\\frac{4}{{e}^{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{4}-4}{{e}^{7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122441/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c33b34e-5b57-51c1-91d0-e098364bcdfb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122441"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122580/selection/f0f45940ed5df71758de7ff31ea171bc0689f380be113b3538530f3180b5105f" :answer/id #uuid "61d88edb-f7f8-599c-a4bf-eaf7c9d0ff0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122580/selection/8b0da25323387be7cd3dda381ee4e2ebbdc8b10be241bc2e3eeead0da24f888a" :answer/id #uuid "860c3d22-ce0e-591a-b810-a7678e5e1f6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122580/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "076c1023-f586-53ab-aa93-9151d67fa434" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122580/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" :answer/id #uuid "5e4275f8-1e72-5fdd-9545-500049bf6a8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122580/selection/b9e37961d17591920349894dfae8783436f581130d0da0bd042142640bfd4f67" :answer/id #uuid "ede80027-e3d1-5048-af45-cefad51b07fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122580/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3403f501-10ad-5e1c-a0a7-52eb157be6e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122580/selection/b9e37961d17591920349894dfae8783436f581130d0da0bd042142640bfd4f67" :answer-field/choices ["q-122580/selection/f0f45940ed5df71758de7ff31ea171bc0689f380be113b3538530f3180b5105f" "q-122580/selection/8b0da25323387be7cd3dda381ee4e2ebbdc8b10be241bc2e3eeead0da24f888a" "q-122580/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-122580/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" "q-122580/selection/b9e37961d17591920349894dfae8783436f581130d0da0bd042142640bfd4f67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122580" :question/id #uuid "45c42586-3a9b-55d5-9072-f51b8fc20108" :question/math-academy-id "q-122580" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=y+1$ along the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $5$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{sin}^{2}⁡t+25{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=y+1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)\\,\\text{d}t & =5[-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t]_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =5[(-5+5)+(2\\pi -0)] \\\\  & =10\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122580/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c33b34e-5b57-51c1-91d0-e098364bcdfb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122580"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40255"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057418/assets/cbd92b205693f1056e4dc2d0fc8154843e62b433b66d9b0ba8918d7f5bb3b8bf.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}$ along the circle $C$ with equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4,$ traversed from the point $(-2,0)$ to the point $(0,-2),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $2$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t & =2{\\int }_{0}^{-2}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2{e}^{u}{|}_{0}^{-2} \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2}-2{e}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{2}}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9438"] :question/problem "Find, as a definite integral, an expression for the line integral of the function $f(x,y) = x^2-1,$ traversed once along the circle $C$ with equation $x^2 + y^2 = 1.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $1$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\big\\langle \\cos{t}, \\: \\sin{t} \\big\\rangle, \\qquad 0 \\le t \\lt 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y) = x^2-1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-1 \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({cos}^{2}⁡t-1)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t-1\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6305"] :question/problem "Find, as a definite integral, an expression for the line integral of the function $f(x,y) = 2x+y^2$ along the quarter-circle $x^2+y^2=4,$ traversed from the point $(0,2)$ to the point $(-2,0)$ in the second quadrant." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a quarter-circle of radius $2$ centered at $O,$ shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057418/assets/d0ae53dd5d0932cbf834a166e851c227f75cb546b591a9fd43930ec06f0e9ddf.png)\n\nThe curve $C$ can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\big\\langle 2\\cos{t}, \\: 2\\sin{t} \\big\\rangle, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\le t \\le \\pi.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y) = 2x+y^2,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(2x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9462"] :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y) =x^2-2$ along the circle $C$ with equation $x^2 + y^2 = 4.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $2$ centered at $O.$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\big\\langle 2\\cos{t}, \\: 2\\sin{t} \\big\\rangle, \\qquad 0 \\le t \\le 2\\pi.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y) = x^2-2,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-2 \\\\  & =4{cos}^{2}⁡t-2 \\\\  & =2(2{cos}^{2}⁡t-1) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=2t,$ $\\textrm d u=2\\,\\textrm d t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t & =2{\\int }_{0}^{4\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{4\\pi } \\\\  & =2(0-0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
